[0.000, "o", "       \"apiVersion\": \"cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1\",\r\n       \"kind\": \"ManagedCluster\",\r\n       \"metadata\": {\r\n         \"creationTimestamp\": \"2026-07-28T04:22:35Z\",\r\n         \"finalizers\": [\r\n           \"cluster.open-cluster-management.io/resource-cleanup\",\r\n           \"cluster.open-cluster-management.io/api-resource-cleanup\"\r\n         ],\r\n         \"generation\": 4,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"managedFields\": [\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "           {\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mlist_addon_placement_scores(cluster1)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mPer-cluster placement scores add-ons publish.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: list_addon_placement_scores\u001b[0m\r\n     No AddOnPlacementScores - no score-publishing add-on runs on this fleet.\r\n"]
[0.009, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mget_pod_logs(cluster1)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mContainer logs from a spoke pod, via the hub-known read context.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_pod_logs\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"namespace\": \"shop\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"pod\": \"payments-5555cb47bc-dn76m\",\r\n       \"log_tail\": \"b'I0728 04:26:47.541306       1 log.go:245] Started HTTP server on port 8080\\\\nI0728 04:26:47.541434       1 log.go:245] Started UDP server on port  8081\\\\nI0728 04:26:49.637957       1 log.go:245] GET /healthz\\\\nI0728 04:26:55.714584       1 log.go:245] GET /healthz\\\\n'\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     }\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mget_hosted_cluster(demo-hcp)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mOne HyperShift hosted control plane in detail.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_hosted_cluster\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     {\r\n       \"name\": \"demo-hcp\",\r\n       \"namespace\": \"clusters\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"version\": \"4.16.7\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"version_state\": \"Completed\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"conditions\": {\r\n         \"Available\": \"True\"\r\n       },\r\n       \"node_pools\": [\r\n         {\r\n           \"name\": \"demo-hcp-workers\",\r\n           \"namespace\": \"clusters\",\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mpropose_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe agent PROPOSES a change. It must pass static guardrails and a Kyverno dry-run first; nothing is applied yet.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: propose_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     proposal_id=518d6215329144be8d7fba9702d14276\r\n     status=pending_approval\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mapply with a BAD token\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mProve the gate holds: apply with an invalid token must be refused by the server, not applied.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_manifestwork(bad token)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     REJECTED: Malformed approval token.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mocm-mcp approve (human)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA human on a trusted terminal mints an approval token: an Ed25519 signature binding the exact content and operation. The server holds only the public key, so it can verify a token but can never mint one - and neither can the agent.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ ocm-mcp approve 518d6215329144be8d7fba9702d14276\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     token minted (...-4EFsDNMJ8Aw)\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mapply_manifestwork(token)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mWith a valid token, the server verifies it and delivers the change as an OCM ManifestWork.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\",\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"manifestwork\": \"e2e-demo\",\r\n       \"note\": \"Verify rollout with get_cluster_health / get_manifestwork. To undo, call propose_rollback then apply the rollback with a fresh approval.\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[5.003, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mget_manifestwork (verify)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mConfirm the hub actually applied it on the spoke.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"name\": \"e2e-demo\",\r\n       \"conditions\": {\r\n         \"Applied\": \"True\",\r\n         \"Available\": \"True\"\r\n       },\r\n       \"resources\": [\r\n         {\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "           \"resource\": \"ConfigMap/ocm-mcp-e2e\",\r\n           \"namespace\": \"shop\",\r\n           \"conditions\": {\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mpropose_rollback\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe agent proposes UNDOING the applied change. This creates a distinct proposal bound to the exact ManifestWork name and UID - an old apply token can never delete a workload.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: propose_rollback\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"rollback_proposal_id\": \"c14aa41ee1374912939b7ffca55de18b\",\r\n       \"status\": \"pending_approval\",\r\n       \"next_step\": \"Ask the human operator to run: ocm-mcp approve c14aa41ee1374912939b7ffca55de18b and give you the token, then call rollback_manifestwork(c14aa41ee1374912939b7ffca55de18b, <token>).\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     }\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mrollback with an APPLY token\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mProve operation binding: a token minted for 'apply' must be refused for a rollback.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: rollback_manifestwork(apply-scoped token)\u001b[0m\r\n     REJECTED: This token authorizes 'apply', not 'rollback'.\r\n"]
[0.009, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mrollback_manifestwork(token)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mWith a rollback-scoped token, the server removes the ManifestWork it created.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: rollback_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"status\": \"rolled_back\",\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"manifestwork\": \"e2e-demo\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[4.009, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mverify rollback\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe e2e-demo ManifestWork no longer exists on the hub.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_manifestwork(cluster1, e2e-demo)\u001b[0m\r\n     ManifestWork removed - rollback confirmed.\r\n"]
[0.014, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mpropose_cluster_action(cordon)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mPropose adding a NoSelect taint so Placements stop scheduling here - still gated by approval.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: propose_cluster_action\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"proposal_id\": \"8d5b18ff2585472395356080a8e67862\",\r\n       \"status\": \"pending_approval\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"action\": \"cordon\",\r\n       \"next_step\": \"Ask the human operator to run: ocm-mcp approve 8d5b18ff2585472395356080a8e67862 and provide you the approval token, then call apply_cluster_action.\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.015, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mapply_cluster_action(cordon)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mApplied after approval; the taint now keeps new work off this cluster.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action\u001b[0m\r\n     taints=[{\"effect\": \"NoSelect\", \"key\": \"ocm-mcp-server.io/cordoned\", \"timeAdded\": \"2026-07-28T04:27:05Z\", \"value\": \"true\"}]\r\n"]
[0.023, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36muncordon (restore)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mRemove the taint so the cluster is schedulable again.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(uncordon)\u001b[0m\r\n     taints_after=[]\r\n"]
[0.017, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mset_label (gated)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mStamp a fleet label through the same propose/approve gate - labels drive Placements, so they are write-gated too.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(set_label)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"action\": \"set_label\",\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36maccept (gated, idempotent)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mRe-assert hubAcceptsClient on an already-accepted cluster - exercises the accept path without changing fleet state.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(accept)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"action\": \"accept\",\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\",\r\n       \"approved_csrs\": []\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     }\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36menable_addon (gated)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mCreate a ManagedClusterAddOn through the gate.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(enable_addon)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"action\": \"enable_addon\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"status\": \"applied\",\r\n       \"addon\": \"e2e-demo-addon\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mdisable_addon (gated, cleanup)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mDelete the same ManagedClusterAddOn through the gate - leaving the fleet exactly as we found it.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(disable_addon)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"action\": \"disable_addon\",\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\",\r\n       \"addon\": \"e2e-demo-addon\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: diagnose_fleet\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: diagnose_fleet\u001b[0m\r\n     You are operating a Kubernetes fleet through the OCM hub. Investigate only - do not propose or apply anything yet.\r\n     \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     1. Call list_clusters to see availability, version, and capacity of every cluster.\r\n     2. Call get_addon_health to spot Degraded or unavailable add-ons across the fleet.\r\n     3. For any cluster that is Unavailable or not joined, call get_cluster to read its conditions, then get_cluster_health for unhealthy pods and degraded deployments.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     4. For each unhealthy workload, use query_events and get_pod_logs to find the cause.\r\n     5. Produce a concise report: per cluster, what is wrong, the evidence, and the smallest safe remediation you would propose. Do not act on it yet.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: remediate_with_approval\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: remediate_with_approval\u001b[0m\r\n     A fleet operator reports: payments degraded on cluster1\r\n     \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     Follow the safe remediation workflow:\r\n     1. Investigate with the read tools (list_clusters, get_cluster_health, query_events, get_pod_logs, get_manifestwork) until you can name the root cause with evidence.\r\n     2. Decide the smallest change that fixes it. For a workload change, call propose_manifestwork with pinned images and a precise summary. For a cluster lifecycle change (cordon, uncordon, set a label, accept a cluster), call propose_cluster_action.\r\n     3. If the proposal is REJECTED by static guardrails or Kyverno, read the reason, correct the manifest, and propose again. Never try to bypass a rejection.\r\n     4. Tell the operator the proposal id \r\n     ... (truncated)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: why_not_scheduled\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: why_not_scheduled\u001b[0m\r\n     Explain why cluster 'cluster1' was or was not selected by Placement 'demo-all' in namespace 'default'. Use only reads:\r\n     \r\n     1. get_placement_decision('demo-all', 'default') for the clusters actually chosen.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     2. list_placements to read the Placement's clusterSets and selection intent.\r\n     3. get_cluster('cluster1') for its labels, ClusterClaims, and taints.\r\n     4. list_cluster_set_bindings to confirm the Placement's namespace is bound to the ClusterSet the cluster belongs to.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. list_addon_placement_scores('cluster1') if the Placement uses AddOn prioritizers.\r\n     6. Conclude with the specific reason: not in a bound ClusterSet, failed a predicate, carries a NoSelect taint, or simply out-scored by others.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: incident_postmortem\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: incident_postmortem\u001b[0m\r\n     Write a post-incident report for the change just completed. Base every statement on evidence, not recollection:\r\n     \r\n     1. Call get_audit_trail to retrieve the ordered record of tool calls.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     2. Reconstruct the timeline: what was inspected, what was proposed, which proposal was approved, and what was applied or rolled back.\r\n     3. State the root cause, the remediation, and how recovery was verified.\r\n     4. Note any proposals that were rejected and why, as evidence the guardrails held.\r\n     5. Keep it factual and concise. If the audit log does not support a claim, do not make it.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: onboard_cluster\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: onboard_cluster\u001b[0m\r\n     A new cluster 'cluster1' is trying to join the hub. Onboard it safely:\r\n     \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     1. Call list_pending_csrs to see the pending cluster-join CSRs and confirm one belongs to 'cluster1'.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     2. Call get_cluster('cluster1') to check its current acceptance and conditions.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. Propose acceptance: propose_cluster_action('cluster1', 'accept', <summary>). This sets hubAcceptsClient and approves the pending join CSRs, but applies nothing yet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     4. Give the operator the proposal id, ask them to run `ocm-mcp approve <id>`, and wait for the token.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. Call apply_cluster_action with the token, then verify with get_cluster and get_addon_health that the cluster becomes Available and its agents register.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: addon_troubleshoot\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: addon_troubleshoot\u001b[0m\r\n     The 'governance-policy-framework' add-on looks unhealthy somewhere in the fleet. Investigate without changing anything:\r\n     \r\n     1. Call get_addon_health to find every cluster where an add-on is Degraded or not Available, and confirm which clusters have 'governance-policy-framework' unhealthy.\r\n     2. For each affected cluster, call list_addons_for_cluster(cluster) for the add-on's install namespace and conditions.\r\n     3. Call list_cluster_management_addons to read the fleet-level install strategy for 'governance-policy-framework'.\r\n     4. If a spoke context is configured, use get_cluster_health, query_events, and get_pod_logs in the add-on's install namespace to find the root cause.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. Report the affected cluste\r\n     ... (truncated)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: hosted_cluster_health\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: hosted_cluster_health\u001b[0m\r\n     Assess the health of hosted cluster 'demo-hcp'. Reads only:\r\n     \r\n     1. Call list_hosted_clusters to locate it and read its version and conditions. If the HostedCluster API is not on this hub, the HCP is hosted elsewhere - fall back to the ManagedCluster view with get_cluster('demo-hcp') and get_cluster_info('demo-hcp').\r\n     2. Call get_hosted_cluster(name, namespace) for its version history, control-plane conditions, and node pools.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. Check the NodePools' desired vs current replicas for capacity or scaling problems.\r\n     4. Cross-check the spoke side: get_cluster('demo-hcp') for hub availability and get_addon_health for its add-ons.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. Summarize: control-plane state, worker capacity, and anything degraded,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     ... (truncated)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: policy_compliance_report\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: policy_compliance_report\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     Produce a governance compliance report for the fleet. Reads only:\r\n     \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     1. Call list_policy_violations for every NonCompliant or Pending policy-cluster pair.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     2. Call list_policies for the full picture, including which policies are inform vs enforce (remediationAction).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. Group the violations by policy and by cluster; call out anything Pending separately from NonCompliant.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     4. For the highest-impact violations, note whether the policy is inform (visibility only) or enforce (actively remediating).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. Present a concise table and a short prioritized list of what to fix first. Propose no changes - this is a report.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: capacity_report\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: capacity_report\u001b[0m\r\n     Report on fleet capacity so an operator can place new workloads well. Reads only:\r\n     \r\n     1. Call list_clusters for each cluster's capacity and availability.\r\n     2. Call get_cluster on the candidates to compare capacity against allocatable.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. Where available, call get_cluster_info for node counts and per-node capacity, and list_addon_placement_scores for any custom scores prioritizers use.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     4. Rank clusters by headroom; flag any that are Unavailable, cordoned (NoSelect taint), or nearly full.\r\n     5. Recommend where a new workload should land, and note any cluster that needs attention before it can take more.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: rollout_status\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: rollout_status\u001b[0m\r\n     Report the rollout status of ManifestWorkReplicaSet 'demo-mwrs' in namespace 'default'. Reads only:\r\n     \r\n     1. Call list_manifestworkreplicasets to read its summary (total / applied / available / progressing / degraded) and conditions.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     2. Identify the Placement it targets, then call get_placement_decision to list the clusters in scope.\r\n     3. For any cluster that looks stuck, call get_manifestwork(cluster, <name>) to read the per-resource conditions and status feedback and find what is blocking Apply/Available.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     4. Summarize progress across the fleet and name the specific clusters and resources that are not yet healthy, with evidence.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mlist_pending_proposals\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mProposals still awaiting human approval.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: list_pending_proposals\u001b[0m\r\n     []\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mget_audit_trail\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe append-only log of every tool call so far - the agent writes its incident report from this record, not from memory.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_audit_trail\u001b[0m\r\n     [\r\n     {\"tool\": \"apply_cluster_action\", \"args\": {\"proposal_id\": \"e4266eeb96d1469089794a5c731c49f7\", \"approval_token\": \"<redacted>\"}, \"outcome\": \"ok\", \"error\": \"\", \"duration_ms\": 7, \"ts\": 1785212825.566769, \"actor\": \"sandeepbazar:35621\", \"seq\": 15, \"prev\": \"9a4148d79fdb2c3c3cef4317144452e6f7072307eb6cf6e4174cda9cd60e770a\", \"hash\": \"e49d6908afe2076daf0a8eea3bc7f6dd0fdce8a117532c54dae210b19a9ae68b\"},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     {\"tool\": \"propose_cluster_action\", \"args\": {\"cluster\": \"cluster1\", \"action\": \"accept\", \"summary\": \"accept (gated, idempotent)\", \"params_json\": \"{}\"}, \"outcome\": \"ok\", \"error\": \"\", \"duration_ms\": 7, \"ts\": 1785212825.576585, \"actor\": \"sandeepbazar:35621\", \"seq\": 16, \"prev\": \"e49d6908afe2076daf0a8eea3bc7f6dd0fdce8a117532c54dae210b19a9ae68b\", \"hash\": \"7efe35e49168ce25c38bb3913c2612a0359c113db2221f2836c83f8a60971b22\"},\r\n     {\"tool\": \"apply_cluster_action\", \"args\": {\"proposal_id\": \"25d762ebd5b64594a1a67f061e31ef4c\", \"approval_token\": \"<redacted>\"}, \"outcome\": \"ok\", \"error\": \"\", \"duration_ms\": 8, \"ts\": 1785212825.585314, \"actor\": \"sandeepbazar:35621\", \"seq\": 17, \"prev\": \"7efe35e49168ce25c38bb3913c2612a0359c113db2221f2836c83f8a60971b22\", \"hash\": \"82b448641dbe94cf808e98f9e4f4da9a484b79efcf9d2d533d126814207b9f62\"},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     {\"tool\": \"propose_cluster_action\", \"args\": {\"cluster\": \"cluster1\", \"action\": \"enable_addon\", \"summary\": \"enable_addon (gated)\", \"params_json\": \"{\\\"addon\\\": \\\"e2e-demo-addon\\\"}\"}, \"outcome\": \"o\r\n"]
