[0.065, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mstdio JSON-RPC session\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mSpawn the real server binary, complete the MCP handshake, and verify the full advertised surface (34 tools with safety annotations, 10 prompts, 6 resources) plus a tool call, a resource read, and a prompt over the wire.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp.client.stdio -> ocm-mcp-server\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"server\": \"ocm-mcp-server\",\r\n       \"tools\": 34,\r\n       \"read_annotation_ok\": true,\r\n       \"apply_annotation_ok\": true,\r\n       \"prompts\": 10,\r\n       \"resources\": 6,\r\n       \"guardrails_resource_ok\": true,\r\n       \"list_clusters_over_wire\": true,\r\n       \"prompt_over_wire_ok\": true\r\n     }\r\n"]
[2.013, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mexpired token refused\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA token past its TTL must be rejected even though proposal and content are valid.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ apply_manifestwork(expired token)\u001b[0m\r\n     REJECTED: Approval token has expired; request a fresh approval.\r\n"]
[0.008, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mfresh token still applies\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mSame proposal, fresh token: applies - proving the expiry rejection was about the token, not the content.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ apply_manifestwork(fresh token)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\",\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"manifestwork\": \"e2e-negative\",\r\n       \"note\": \"Verify rollout with get_cluster_health / get_manifestwork. To undo, call propose_rollback then apply the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mreplayed token refused\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe just-spent token must never work twice.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ apply_manifestwork(replayed token)\u001b[0m\r\n     REJECTED: proposal 7105aed1db35407ea4b79486ae8be021 is 'applied', not pending.\r\n"]
[0.441, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mread-only mode refuses writes\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mWith OCM_MCP_READ_ONLY=1 every write tool refuses before any guardrail or token logic runs - the coarse backstop.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ OCM_MCP_READ_ONLY=1 propose_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     REJECTED: this server runs in read-only mode (OCM_MCP_READ_ONLY). No proposals or writes are accepted.\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36maudit chain + signed anchor\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe genuine log verifies; a log with one rewritten entry fails; and a chain head signed by the off-box key (audit-anchor) verifies - so mid-log edits AND tail truncation are both detectable.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ audit-verify / tamper copy / audit-anchor\u001b[0m\r\n     real: audit chain intact over 30 entries\r\n     tampered copy: audit chain broken at line 16 (seq 16)\r\n     anchors: 1 anchor(s) verified; log head is seq 30, last anchored seq 30 (0 newer entries not yet anchored)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "ocm-mcp doctor - live read-path smoke test\r\nhub context: kind-hub\r\n\r\n"]
