[0.093, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;35m[INJECT]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mINJECT: failing-rollout\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mDeploy a 'payments-v2' with a broken image tag, exactly the kind of bad rollout that pages someone at 2 a.m.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ ./chaos/inject.sh failing-rollout cluster1\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     deployment.apps/payments-v2 created\r\n     injected: failing-rollout into cluster1\r\n"]
[12.026, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mDIAGNOSE: get_cluster_health\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe agent asks 'what is unhealthy here?' and sees payments-v2 is not running.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_cluster_health(cluster1)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"unhealthy_pods\": [\r\n         {\r\n           \"namespace\": \"shop\",\r\n           \"name\": \"payments-v2-6f6596d897-mlcb9\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "           \"phase\": \"Pending\",\r\n           \"waiting\": [\r\n             \"ErrImagePull\"\r\n           ],\r\n           \"restarts\": 0\r\n         },\r\n         {\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mDIAGNOSE: query_events\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mEvents reveal the root cause in plain English: the image cannot be pulled.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: query_events(cluster1, shop)\u001b[0m\r\n     [\r\n       {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"namespace\": \"shop\",\r\n         \"type\": \"Normal\",\r\n         \"reason\": \"BackOff\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"object\": \"Pod/payments-v2-6f6596d897-rg978\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"count\": 1,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"message\": \"Back-off pulling image \\\"registry.k8s.io/e2e-test-images/agnhost:2.47-nonexistent\\\"\"\r\n       },\r\n       {\r\n         \"namespace\": \"shop\",\r\n         \"type\": \"Warning\",\r\n"]
[0.006, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m[FIX]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mFIX: propose + approve\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe agent proposes the smallest safe fix (a pinned, known-good image). It clears the guardrails and a human approves it.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ propose_manifestwork -> ocm-mcp approve\u001b[0m\r\n     proposal_id=cf2c34fe715349aa926aca31e534c35f\r\n     guardrails=passed  kyverno_dry_run=passed  approved=yes\r\n"]
[0.007, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m[FIX]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mFIX: apply_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mDelivered to the cluster through the hub as a ManifestWork.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_manifestwork(token)\u001b[0m\r\n     status=applied\r\n"]
[6.018, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mVERIFY: recovery\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mRe-read health until payments-v2 is running again - the incident is closed, with a full audit trail of everything that happened.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_cluster_health(cluster1)\u001b[0m\r\n     payments-v2 is Running again - fix confirmed end to end.\r\n"]
